task: intent-jmh-row
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-05
branch: feature/intent-jmh-row
worktree: ../okay-wt-jmh

why: this line quotes microseconds everywhere — 76us probe, 90us
  centroid, 92us chargrams — and every one of them is a
  `System.nanoTime` around a loop inside a test: no warmup, no JIT
  accounting, one run, on whatever the box was doing. The repository
  keeps `src/jmh/history.tsv` for exactly this and gates benchmark
  claims on it. By its own standard those numbers are not
  measurements, and I have quoted them.

what: JMH benchmarks for what a caller actually pays — classify
  latency per tier through the shipped path, the fit cost at a stated
  row count, and the LOAD cost of the shipped artifact, which is on
  every startup path and has never been measured at all. Then the
  quoted numbers get replaced by the measured ones or removed.

box protocol: this is the first lane to use the rule I proposed after
  colliding with a sibling — announce before taking the box, announce
  when free.
